WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.122
The contribution is two-fold.

00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:08.324
First, the authors present simple,

00:00:08.404 --> 00:00:12.527
easy-to-implement methods that sit on top of a
state-of-the-art VQA framework and maintain

00:00:12.607 --> 00:00:16.729
VQA accuracy while generating human-readable
textual explanations.

00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:20.931
Second,

00:00:21.011 --> 00:00:25.133
they provide both quantitative experimental results
and a large human study of the proposed explainable VQA method.

00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:29.336
Together these illustrate the urgency of proposing
new metrics to evaluate predicted explanations

00:00:29.416 --> 00:00:33.538
in vision-language reasoning problems like VQA,

00:00:33.618 --> 00:00:37.740
since the metrics in common use today do not
reliably reflect explanation quality.
